      <dc:creator>Amarjeet Singh</dc:creator>
      <!-- Description: executive summary or first key takeaway only (no full HTML body).
           This keeps the RSS file small and avoids duplicate-content issues with Google. -->
      <description><![CDATA[
        Middle East war disruptions and Ukrainian strikes on Russian refineries drove India and China to absorb over 80% of Russia’s crude exports. But with surging premiums, can this Eurasian energy surge endure past 2026?
        
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ Ukrainian strikes disabled nearly 50% of Russian refining capacity, forcing Moscow to export unrefined crude to maintain revenue.
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ Surging ESPO spot premiums of up to $30/bbl over Brent are pricing out China&#39;s independent &#39;teapot&#39; refiners.
        [SPLIT]
